      "content": "the last part got cut off but i get what u mean. so u're basically saying the main legal argument is just that there's no precedent? that seems a bit weak compared to the arguments for it. is there any actual logic the opposition uses regarding individual vs collective responsibility, or is it mostly just about the fact that it would be way too complicated to figure out who gets what?",
      "source": "evaluator"
